{"title":"2021 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems#Problem_12\" title=\"2021 AMC 10B Problems\">2021 AMC 10B #12</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems#Problem_7\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems\">2021 AMC 12B #7</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Simplest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Simplest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Under_2_min!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Under 2 min!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Prime_Factorization)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Prime Factorization)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/5/6b5fdc3950f2fbdbd20edacedd030310d90198d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 34 \\cdot 34 \\cdot 63 \\cdot 270$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"161\" height=\"13\" />. What is the ratio of the sum of the odd divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to the sum of the even divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d5266919c06342869393f377d0073a29ac757a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~1 : 16 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~1 : 15 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~1 : 14 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)} ~1 : 8 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~1 : 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"497\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Simplest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Simplest)\">Solution 1 (Simplest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Simplest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prime factorize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/30174004e27032c62f900010dd0588a140572690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=2^{3} \\cdot 3^{5} \\cdot 5\\cdot 7\\cdot 17^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"168\" height=\"15\" />. For each odd divisor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, there exist even divisors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a1b0d8a11c2bf104d34c6a50f641ac6ac4c2c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/5/2857cee2bb4600325f3e680ddcf01b9a837c0a9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88f825e8eca022f48ac1d2d41cd80ad6e5d9ef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, therefore the ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e29b79f5b78ec4bec3af650428306a205105124.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1:(2+4+8)=\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} ~1 : 14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"224\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~FlynnH(grammar edits)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The formula of the sum of the prime factors does not work in this question.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prime factorizing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, we see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/30174004e27032c62f900010dd0588a140572690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=2^{3} \\cdot 3^{5} \\cdot 5\\cdot 7\\cdot 17^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"168\" height=\"15\" />.\nThe sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />'s odd divisors are the sum of the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> without <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and the sum of the even divisors is the sum of the odds subtracted by the total sum of divisors. \n</p><p>BY SUM OF FACTORS FORMULA (search it up if you don't know): \nThe formula is actually for all factors, but we can just take out the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f6a4ab443c94f13ae3ad0efbc8c6fa07b58a930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, so we have:\n</p><p>The sum of odd divisors is given by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d43ad58db14705adb3a80482071db62edeed9039.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = (1+3+3^2 + 3^3 + 3^4 + 3^5)(1 + 5)(1+7)(1+17+17^2)\\]\" width=\"462\" height=\"19\" /> and the total sum of divisors is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/8/988f4d1d96ecf8b5b835d9022bec978c99e51fa1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1+2+4+8)(1+3+3^2 + 3^3 + 3^4 + 3^5)(1 + 5)(1+7)(1+17+17^2) = 15a.\\]\" width=\"504\" height=\"19\" /> Thus, our ratio is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb40e0665d665311e990a490d8a6e57c429ab3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{a}{15a-a} = \\frac{a}{14a} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} ~1 : 14}.\\]\" width=\"233\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~JustinLee2017\n~WhySean38\n~minor edits by SwordAxe\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Prime factorizing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, we have that there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f6a4ab443c94f13ae3ad0efbc8c6fa07b58a930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> in our factorization. Now, call the sum of the odd divisors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. We know that if we multiply k by 2, we will have even divisors. So, we can multiply k by 2, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d76f405f09f15a3cfb0d5ea56c3c776d2813b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2, 2^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" /> respectively to get 14k as the sum of the even divisors. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/4/7e4175012eb8df69ee6690553f76c7875ae49837.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{k}{14k} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)} ~1:14}.\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"37\" />\n~MC\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Under_2_min.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Under_2_min!)\">Video Solution (Under 2 min!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Under 2 min!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/AiWQjjL85ZE\">https://youtu.be/AiWQjjL85ZE</a>\n</p><p><i>~Education, the Study of Everything </i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=qpvS2PVkI8A&amp;t=643s\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=qpvS2PVkI8A&amp;t=643s</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Prime_Factorization.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Prime_Factorization)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Prime Factorization)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Prime Factorization)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/U3msAYWeMbI\">https://youtu.be/U3msAYWeMbI</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Hawk Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VzwxbsuSQ80\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VzwxbsuSQ80</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/L1iW94Ue3eI?t=478\">https://youtu.be/L1iW94Ue3eI?t=478</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/duZG-jirKRc\">https://youtu.be/duZG-jirKRc</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B\">2021 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2